      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think the images aren't compressed at all and some people use 2k resolution or even more for vrc+ profile pictures.  Also VRCX (third party program for managing friendships in VRChat) allows you upload quite high resolution thumbnails for avatars as well. VRChat could implement server sided compression like most websites do where users have custom avatars for their profiles. If I recall correctly steam avatar sizes for use in game come only in 32, 64 etc, in a web browser max size is 128x128.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
